### Assistant
Found it.

**`74f34f68` (2026-09-09)** — "notmuch: 0 removes every tag via --remove-all; shorter marked-footer captions" (the jj description is stale; the diff is the dismiss work). It added:

- `apps/compos_core/priv/packages/dismiss.scm` (new, 185 lines) — `dismiss-mode` binding `q` → `dismiss-buffer`, synced on `post-command-hook` / `window-configuration-change-hook`, plus advice on `set-mode!` and `buffer-set-read-only!`
- `editor_live.ex:1794` — the `<div class="dismiss-bar">` with `<span class="dismiss-title">Reading</span>` and the `q` Back button
- `layouts.ex:483` — `.window.dismissible` outline
- `editor.ex:3133` — `dismissible` and `cursor_visible` in the snapshot

Duplicate copies of the same change are in this tree as `806fdee9` and `45ac86d3`.

The older, related one is **`9c6df010` (2026-08-14)** "editor: q quits every read-only buffer" — that added the `" *read-only*"` keymap layer with `q` → `quit-window` (`editor.scm:8336`).

On the minibuffer bug: the key ladder itself is minibuffer-aware — `editor.ex:2500` and `2663` both use `minibuf_of(f)` when a prompt is open, so the read-only layer keys off the *minibuf* buffer, not the window's buffer. And the live minibuf buffer is not flagged right now:

```
(buffer-read-only? " *minibuf-f-tgfe72q*")  ; => #f
```

The path that fits is `(current-buffer)` redirecting to the minibuf while a prompt is open (`editor.ex:849`), so any mode setup that runs during a prompt — list-mode setup at `editor.scm:8507`, `collect-mode` at `2161`, peek at `7417` — does `(buffer-set-read-only! (current-buffer) #t)` on the minibuffer, and it sticks (read-only is checkpointed, `buffer.ex:1010`).

Want me to add the guard — `buffer-set-read-only!` and `dismiss--sync!` refuse a `" *minibuf-*"` buffer, so reading presentation applies to buffers only?

### Status
A commit adds a `q` key to the minibuffer to quit read-only buffers.

