     (if other-window? \\\"Other window buffer: \\\" \\\"Switch to: \\\"))\\n            (switch-prompt-rows rows)\\n            ;; the invoking window live-previews the highlighted buffer; a\\n            ;; card or a tab leaves the window alone. The primitive wakes a\\n            ;; sleeper; the mode setup must follow, or switch-to-buffer!\\n            ;; later sees the buffer live and skips its own restore\\n            (lambda (label)\\n              (let ((b (switch-prompt-name rows label)))\\n                (when (buffer-known? b)\\n                  (let ((sleeping (not (buffer-exists? b))))\\n                    (window-preview-buffer! b)\\n                    (when (and sleeping (buffer-exists? b))\\n                      (restore-buffer-runtime! b)\\n                      (set! woken (cons b woken)))))))\\n            (lambda (name)\\n              (let* ((context? (let ((x *mb-confirm-context*))\\n                                 (set! *mb-confirm-context* #f)\\n                                 x))\\n                     (picked (if (equal? name \\\"\\\")\\n                                 (or fallback \\\"\\\")\\n                                 (switch-prompt-name rows name)))\\n                     (e (row-of picked)))\\n                (cond\\n                  ((equal? picked \\\"\\\") #f)\\n                  ((buffer-known? picked)\\n\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01T62xPN8qKzVDn9PvWky3ZM","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (list (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn 'with_current_buffer\\\\\\\\|with-current-buffer' apps/compos_core/lib/compos/scheme/*.ex | head -20\\\" root)\\n        (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn 'restore-buffer-runtime!' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm | head -5\\\" root)))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01T62xPN8qKzVDn9PvWky3ZM","(\"grep: apps/compos_core/lib/compos/scheme/*.ex: No such file or directory\\n\" \"apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:3287:    (for-each restore-buffer-runtime! bufs)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:3336:;; buffers rebuilt. restore-buffer-runtime! is desktop restore's entry: it\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:3342:    (for-each restore-buffer-runtime! bs)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:3955:(define (restore-buffer-runtime! buf)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:4319:    (when restoring (restore-buffer-runtime! buf))\\n\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01KMxGpdZXYXTy7kMqwuse1d","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (list (shell-command->string \\\"sed -n '3955,3990p' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm\\\" root)\\n        (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn 'with-current-buffer' apps/compos_core/lib -r | head -10\\\" root)))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01KMxGpdZXYXTy7kMqwuse1d","(\"(define (restore-buffer-runtime! buf)\\n  (with-layout-suppressed\\n    (lambda ()\\n      (with-current-buffer buf\\n        (lambda ()\\n          (with-buffer-waking\\n            (lambda ()\\n              (let ((mode (buffer-local buf 'mode-name)))\\n                (when mode (set-mode! mode)))\\n              (restore-minor-modes! buf)\\n              ;; a restored popup floats still, so its move keys come back\\n              (when (popup--class? buf) (popup-keys! buf #t))))))))\\n  ;; The modeline is derived state. Rebuild it here so a restored desktop\\n  ;; shows its top line and its short name before the first command runs.\\n  (when (boundp (quote dashboard--sync!))\\n    (dashboard--sync! buf))\\n  ;; The buffer is whole again, so an owner can act on it. Outside\\n  ;; with-buffer-waking on purpose: that flag is restored by hand, and a\\n  ;; hook that throws inside it would leave every later wake believing it\\n  ;; was still waking.\\n  (buffer-woken! buf))\\n\\n;;; Visual lines are a buffer capability, independent of the major mode.\\n;;; This minor mode owns the durable flag. The client measures where the\\n;;; rendered rows begin and reports the byte offsets per window, tagged\\n;;; with the buffer version it measured: the wrap map. The client cannot\\n;;; know what a key means on those rows; that is decided here.\\n\\n(domain! 'interaction)\\n(effects! '(write))\\n\\n(define (visual-line-mode--apply! buf)\\n  (buffer-set-local! buf 'visual-line-mode #t))\\n\\n(define (visual-line-mode--teardown! buf)\\n  (buffer-set-local! buf 'visual-line-mode #f)\\n\" \"apps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/session.ex:1165:      \\\"with-current-buffer\\\" =>\\napps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/session.ex:1166:        \\\"(with-current-buffer BUF THUNK) — run THUNK with BUF current without displaying it or changing any window.\\\",\\napps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/session.ex:2324:      \\\"with-current-buffer\\\" => fn [buffer, thunk], store ->\\n\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01MfMGNs18KLZjGQKAwE2C8i","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (shell-command->string \\\"sed -n '2318,2360p' apps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/session.ex\\\" root))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01MfMGNs18KLZjGQKAwE2C8i","\"      end,\\n      \\\"current-edit-author\\\" => fn [] -> Process.get(:compos_edit_author) || false end,\\n      # Emacs' logical current-buffer binding, deliberately separate from\\n      # window display. Tool evaluation uses this so visit/switch operations\\n      # can establish the buffer commands act on without hijacking the user's\\n      # selected window.\\n      \\\"with-current-buffer\\\" => fn [buffer, thunk], store ->\\n        buffer = to_string(buffer)\\n\\n        unless Compos.Core.Buffer.exists?(buffer) do\\n          raise Compos.Scheme.Eval.Error, message: \\\"no such buffer: \\#{buffer}\\\"\\n        end\\n\\n        Compos.Core.Frame.with_buffer(buffer, fn ->\\n          Compos.Scheme.Eval.apply_fn(thunk, [], store)\\n        end)\\n      end,\\n      # The deliberate exit from that binding. Inside the thunk,\\n      # current-buffer and the switch primitives resolve through the\\n      # frame's real windows, so a tool that intends a display change can\\n      # make one and observe it truthfully.\\n      \\\"buffer-context?\\\" => fn [] -> Frame.buffer_context() != nil end,\\n      \\\"with-frame-windows\\\" => fn [thunk], store ->\\n        Compos.Core.Frame.without_buffer(fn ->\\n          Compos.Scheme.Eval.apply_fn(thunk, [], store)\\n        end)\\n      end,\\n      # Scheme tasks share global bindings. This narrow lock lets Scheme\\n      # publish an expensive derived value once after shared source changes.\\n      # The process identity keeps :global's requester identity distinct.\\n      \\\"with-scheme-lock\\\" => fn [key, thunk], store ->\\n        lock = {{__MODULE__, :scheme_lock, key}, self()}\\n\\n        :global.trans(lock, fn ->\\n          # A waiting eval can hold shared reads from before the lock. Refresh\\n          # them so the critical section sees the previous owner's writes.\\n          Compos.Scheme.Env.forget_cached_reads()\\n          Compos.Scheme.Eval.apply_fn(thunk, [], store)\\n        end)\\n      end,\\n      # (wait-until PRED &optional TIMEOUT-MS INTERVAL-MS) -> #t | #f\\n      #\\n      # Wait for work that is not on this lane: a subprocess handshake, a\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01JMGHzEaZmNr2opJJcDK8De","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (shell-command->string \\\"sed -n '2863,2900p' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm\\\" root))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01JMGHzEaZmNr2opJJcDK8De","\"(define (minibuffer-read-preview prompt cands on-select on-confirm on-cancel\\n                                 &optional match-hint style complete collect)\\n  ;; the outer prompt's cancel handler clears *mb-select-fn*, so let it run\\n  ;; BEFORE this prompt installs its own. minibuffer-read* would quit the\\n  ;; outer prompt for us, but by then the new hook is already in place and\\n  ;; the old prompt's teardown takes it away: the new prompt opens with no\\n  ;; preview and no rail, which is the bug this line prevents.\\n  (when (minibuffer-active?)\\n    (minibuffer-cancel!)\\n    (message \\\"Quit the outer prompt\\\"))\\n  (set! *mb-select-fn* (lambda (sel) (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (on-select sel)))))\\n  (minibuffer-read* prompt cands\\n    (append\\n      (list (list 'confirm (lambda (v)\\n                              (set! *mb-select-fn* #f)\\n                              (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (on-confirm v)))))\\n            (list 'cancel  (lambda ()\\n                              (set! *mb-select-fn* #f)\\n                              (with-invoking-buffer on-cancel)))\\n            (list 'change  (lambda (input) (mb-select-notify!)))\\n            (list 'match-hint (if match-hint match-hint #f))\\n            (list 'style style))\\n      (if complete (list (list 'complete complete)) '())\\n      (if collect (list (list 'collect collect)) '()))))\\n\\n(let ((mb (minibuffer-buffer)))\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"M-RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm-input\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"C-RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm-context\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"C-g\\\" \\\"minibuffer-cancel\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"TAB\\\" \\\"minibuffer-complete\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"C-n\\\" \\\"minibuffer-next-candidate\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"<down>\\\" \\\"minibuffer-next-candidate\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"C-p\\\" \\\"minibuffer-previous-candidate\\\")\\n  (local-set-key* mb \\\"<up>\\\" \\\"minibuffer-previous-candidate\\\")\\n  ;; the palette's two lists: <right> steps into the one on the right,\\n  ;; <left> steps back. With no rail they are the point motion they have\\n  ;; always been, and C-f/C-b move point either way\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01SP3Dx8ygukD1npL5MbHJ2s","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (list (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn 'with-invoking-buffer' apps/compos_core/priv --include='*.scm' | grep -v tests | head -20\\\" root)\\n        (shell-command->string \\\"grep -n 'define (with-invoking-buffer' -A 20 apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm\\\" root)))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01SP3Dx8ygukD1npL5MbHJ2s","(\"apps/compos_core/priv/packages/groups.scm:2008:          (with-invoking-buffer\\napps/compos_core/priv/packages/groups.scm:2027:          (with-invoking-buffer\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:1736:        (begin (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (list-move-in! buf step))) #t)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:1747:           (and f (begin (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (f buf))) #t))))))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:1788:               (with-invoking-buffer\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2636:(define (with-invoking-buffer thunk)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2645:;; invoking buffer, not the minibuffer's — see with-invoking-buffer.\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2873:  (set! *mb-select-fn* (lambda (sel) (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (on-select sel)))))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2878:                              (with-invoking-buffer (lambda () (on-confirm v)))))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2881:                              (with-invoking-buffer on-cancel)))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:5349:                    (with-invoking-buffer\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:5366:                      (with-invoking-buffer\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:5373:                            (with-invoking-buffer\\n\" \"2636:(define (with-invoking-buffer thunk)\\n2637-  (set-mb-redirect! #f)\\n2638-  (let ((result (thunk)))\\n2639-    (set-mb-redirect! #t)\\n2640-    result))\\n2641-\\n2642-;; minibuffer-read with live candidate preview: ON-SELECT fires per\\n2643-;; highlight move, ON-CONFIRM with the choice, ON-CANCEL on C-g (restore\\n2644-;; whatever the preview displaced there). All three run against the\\n2645-;; invoking buffer, not the minibuffer's — see with-invoking-buffer.\\n2646-;; One prompt at a time, as in Emacs without enable-recursive-minibuffers.\\n2647-;; A prompt that opens while another is up cancels the outer one first,\\n2648-;; so its cancel handler restores what it displaced, instead of the\\n2649-;; outer prompt vanishing with its closures.\\n2650-(define minibuffer-read*--raw minibuffer-read*)\\n2651-\\n2652-(define (minibuffer-active?) (if (minibuffer-state) #t #f))\\n2653-\\n2654-;; what the prompt holds now, \\\"\\\" without a prompt\\n2655-(define (minibuffer-input)\\n2656-  (let ((st (minibuffer-state)))\\n\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_019UmUqrh24zCSPUTEtVDMYZ","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (shell-command->string \\\"sed -n '2660,2740p' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm\\\" root))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_019UmUqrh24zCSPUTEtVDMYZ","\"  (when (minibuffer-active?)\\n    (minibuffer-cancel!)\\n    (message \\\"Quit the outer prompt\\\"))\\n  ;; a rail belongs to one prompt: the next one starts without it\\n  (mb-rail-reset!)\\n  (minibuffer-read*--raw prompt cands handlers))\\n\\n;; one interaction model: a completion prompt is the BOTTOM bar, like\\n;; Emacs — the candidates sit above the input and the input sits on the\\n;; last row. Only a prompt that asks for \\\"palette\\\" by name floats: the\\n;; switcher, the command palette, and the LLM config menus.\\n;;\\n;; the builtin reads (prompt cands confirm) or (prompt cands complete\\n;; confirm); this wrapper keeps both shapes\\n(define (minibuffer-read prompt cands a &optional b)\\n  (minibuffer-read* prompt cands\\n    (append\\n      (list (list 'confirm (if b b a)))\\n      (if b (list (list 'complete a)) '())\\n      (list (list 'style #f)))))\\n\\n;;; --- completing-read ----------------------------------------------------------\\n;;; Emacs's completing-read, asynchronous: K gets the choice. COLLECTION is\\n;;; a list of candidates (strings or (label hint) rows) or a procedure of\\n;;; the input that answers the rows. OPTS is a plist:\\n;;;   'predicate FN       keep the candidates FN accepts\\n;;;   'require-match #t   RET takes a candidate only; free text says [No match]\\n;;;   'initial TEXT       the input to start with\\n;;;   'default TEXT       the answer to an empty input, listed first\\n;;;   'history SYM        the history to read and to push the choice on\\n;;;   'category SYM       the marginalia annotator to use\\n;;;   'style SYM          how the input matches: flex, substring, prefix, regexp\\n;;;   'annotate? #f       the rows are annotated already\\n\\n(define *mb-history-key* #f)          ; the history the active prompt walks\\n(define *mb-history-pos* -1)          ; -1 is the input, 0 the newest item\\n(define *mb-history-input* \\\"\\\")        ; what was typed before M-p\\n\\n(define (completing-read--rows collection input)\\n  (if (procedure? collection) (collection input) collection))\\n\\n(define (completing-read--label row) (if (pair? row) (car row) row))\\n\\n(define (completing-read--prepare rows opts)\\n  (let* ((pred (plist-get opts 'predicate))\\n         (kept (if pred (filter (lambda (r) (pred (completing-read--label r))) rows) rows))\\n         (default (plist-get opts 'default))\\n         (led (if (and default (member default (map completing-read--label kept)))\\n                  (cons (let loop ((rs kept))\\n                          (if (equal? (completing-read--label (car rs)) default) (car rs) (loop (cdr rs))))\\n                        (filter (lambda (r) (not (equal? (completing-read--label r) default))) kept))\\n                  kept))\\n         (hist (plist-get opts 'history))\\n         (ordered (if (and hist (not (pair? (car (or (and (pair? led) led) '(\\\"\\\")))))) (history-order hist led) led))\\n         (category (plist-get opts 'category)))\\n    (if (and category (not (equal? (plist-get opts 'annotate?) #f)))\\n        (annotate category ordered)\\n        ordered)))\\n\\n(define (completing-read prompt collection k &rest opts)\\n  (let* ((hist (plist-get opts 'history))\\n         (default (plist-get opts 'default))\\n         (require? (plist-get opts 'require-match))\\n         (rows (completing-read--prepare (completing-read--rows collection \\\"\\\") opts))\\n         (labels (lambda () (map completing-read--label\\n                                (completing-read--prepare\\n                                  (completing-read--rows collection (minibuffer-input)) opts))))\\n         (confirm\\n           (lambda (v)\\n             (let ((v (if (and default (equal? v \\\"\\\")) default v)))\\n               (cond ((and require? (not (member v (labels))))\\n                      (message \\\"[No match]\\\")\\n                      (apply completing-read (append (list prompt collection k) opts)))\\n                     (else\\n                       (when hist (history-push! hist v))\\n                       (set! *mb-history-key* #f)\\n                       (k v)))))))\\n    (set! *mb-history-key* hist)\\n    (set! *mb-history-pos* -1)\\n    (minibuffer-read* prompt rows\\n      (append\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01Hw1MyQxwyeNJcSzWr2Uq9V","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (shell-command->string \\\"grep -n 'minibuffer-confirm\\\\\\\\|:confirm\\\\\\\\|mb_close\\\\\\\\|minibuffer: nil' apps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/editor.ex | head -30\\\" root))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01Hw1MyQxwyeNJcSzWr2Uq9V","\"319:  def minibuffer_close(fid \\\\\\\\ nil), do: GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:mb_close, fid(fid)})\\n601:      minibuffer: nil,\\n684:          minibuffer: nil,\\n1663:  def handle_call({:mb_close, fid}, _from, state) do\\n1673:    changed(reply, put_frame(state, %{f | minibuffer: nil}), f.id)\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_013gh2kjb1yVywWsjPSnnHZo","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (list (shell-command->string \\\"grep -n 'minibuffer-confirm\\\\\\\\|minibuffer-close!\\\\\\\\|mb-close' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm | head -20\\\" root)))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_013gh2kjb1yVywWsjPSnnHZo","(\"2543:(define-command \\\"minibuffer-confirm\\\" \\\"Accept the selected minibuffer candidate\\\"\\n2544:  (lambda () (if (mb-rail-confirm!) #t (minibuffer-confirm!))))\\n2551:(define-command \\\"minibuffer-confirm-context\\\"\\n2553:  (lambda () (set! *mb-confirm-context* #t) (minibuffer-confirm!)))\\n2554:(define-command \\\"minibuffer-confirm-input\\\" \\\"Accept the minibuffer input exactly as typed\\\"\\n2555:  (lambda () (minibuffer-confirm-input!)))\\n2889:  (local-set-key* mb \\\"RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm\\\")\\n2890:  (local-set-key* mb \\\"M-RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm-input\\\")\\n2891:  (local-set-key* mb \\\"C-RET\\\" \\\"minibuffer-confirm-context\\\")\\n\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01KnbioELD9Jm7s6uLub6Dya","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (shell-command->string \\\"grep -n 'minibuffer-confirm!' -A 20 apps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/session.ex | head -45\\\" root))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01KnbioELD9Jm7s6uLub6Dya","\"1208:      \\\"minibuffer-confirm!\\\" =>\\n1209:        \\\"(minibuffer-confirm!) — close the prompt; run its confirm handler with the value.\\\",\\n1210-      \\\"minibuffer-confirm-input!\\\" =>\\n1211-        \\\"(minibuffer-confirm-input!) — close the prompt; submit the input, not the candidate.\\\",\\n1212-      \\\"minibuffer-cancel!\\\" =>\\n1213-        \\\"(minibuffer-cancel!) — close the prompt; run its cancel handler; echo Quit.\\\",\\n1214-      \\\"minibuffer-detach!\\\" =>\\n1215-        \\\"(minibuffer-detach!) — close the prompt; return its state and closures, or #f.\\\",\\n1216-      \\\"minibuffer-complete!\\\" =>\\n1217-        \\\"(minibuffer-complete!) — run the prompt's completion, or copy the selection to the input.\\\",\\n1218-      \\\"minibuffer-next!\\\" => \\\"(minibuffer-next!) — move the candidate selection down one.\\\",\\n1219-      \\\"minibuffer-prev!\\\" => \\\"(minibuffer-prev!) — move the candidate selection up one.\\\",\\n1220-      \\\"minibuffer-rail!\\\" =>\\n1221-        \\\"(minibuffer-rail! ROWS INDEX FOCUSED) — set the palette's right-hand list. ROWS is ((LABEL HINT ...) ...), INDEX the row on, FOCUSED whether the arrows are in it; '() clears it.\\\",\\n1222-      \\\"minibuffer-del!\\\" =>\\n1223-        \\\"(minibuffer-del!) — delete one char back; at a directory boundary, delete the component.\\\"\\n1224-    }\\n1225-  end\\n1226-\\n1227-  defp session_primitives(global) do\\n1228-    eval_src = fn src, store ->\\n1229-      Enum.reduce(Compos.Scheme.Reader.read_all(src), {:void, store}, fn form, {_v, store} ->\\n--\\n2634:      \\\"minibuffer-confirm!\\\" => fn [], store ->\\n2635-        case Editor.minibuffer_close() do\\n2636-          %{on_confirm: oc} = mb when oc not in [nil, false] ->\\n2637-            {value, store} = mb_confirm_value(mb, store)\\n2638-            {_, store} = Compos.Scheme.Eval.apply_fn(oc, [value], store)\\n2639-            {:void, store}\\n2640-\\n2641-          _ ->\\n2642-            {:void, store}\\n2643-        end\\n2644-      end,\\n2645-      # M-RET: submit the typed input as-is, ignoring the highlighted\\n2646-      # candidate (vertico-exit-input) — creates files whose names fuzzy-\\n2647-      # match existing ones\\n2648-      \\\"minibuffer-confirm-input!\\\" => fn [], store ->\\n2649-        case Editor.minibuffer_close() do\\n2650-          %{on_confirm: oc} = mb when oc not in [nil, false] ->\\n2651-            {_, store} = Compos.Scheme.Eval.apply_fn(oc, [mb.input], store)\\n2652-            {:void, store}\\n2653-\\n2654-          _ ->\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["text","A commit was made to add a 'q' and 'reading' header to minibuffers."]],"role":"status"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_016cvTi8bQXptbEkbCaqh9Kz","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(let ((root (git-root (default-directory))))\\n  (list (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn \\\\\\\"list 'change\\\\\\\" apps/compos_core/priv --include='*.scm' | grep -v tests | head -20\\\" root)\\n        (shell-command->string \\\"grep -rn 'unwind-protect\\\\\\\\|dynamic-wind' apps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm | head -5\\\" root)))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_016cvTi8bQXptbEkbCaqh9Kz","(\"apps/compos_core/priv/packages/ibuffer.scm:965:      (list (list 'change narrow)\\napps/compos_core/priv/packages/jj.scm:415:               (list 'change change\\napps/compos_core/priv/packages/project.scm:536:        (list (list 'change (project--nav root base))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:1812:        (list (list 'change narrow)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2744:            (list (list 'change\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2799:      (list (list 'change\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2811:      (list (list 'change\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2845:      (list (list 'change\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:2882:            (list 'change  (lambda (input) (mb-select-notify!)))\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:5131:      (list (list 'change\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:5955:                (list 'change file-nav-change)\\napps/compos_core/priv/editor.scm:12257:            (list 'change\\n\" \"\")",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["text","A commit added a 'q' and 'reading' header to minibuffers, which is a bug affecting only these areas."]],"role":"status"},{"blocks":[["text","Yes. The shared root is `mb_redirect` (`editor.ex:849`): while a prompt is open, `current-buffer`, point primitives and the local keymap all resolve to `\" *minibuf-<fid>*\"`. Anything that writes per-buffer state without naming a buffer hits the minibuffer.\n\n**1. `with-invoking-buffer` has no unwind guard.** `editor.scm:2636`:\n\n```scheme\n(define (with-invoking-buffer thunk)\n  (set-mb-redirect! #f)\n  (let ((result (thunk)))\n    (set-mb-redirect! #t)\n    result))\n```\n\nThere is no `unwind-protect` or `dynamic-wind` anywhere in editor.scm. If an on-select raises, redirect stays `#f` for the rest of that prompt, so your keystrokes route to the *window's* buffer instead of the input. When that window holds a read-only buffer (browse, notmuch, any list, i.e. exactly the ones the Reading bar marks), the writes are refused and the prompt reads as read-only. This is my best candidate for the symptom you saw.\n\n**2. Keys and hooks while a prompt is open.** Every command you type in a prompt runs `pre-command-hook` and `post-command-hook` with the minibuf current. `editing--after-command!` (`editor.scm:12938`) takes `(current-buffer)` unguarded, and the live minibuf shows the result:\n\n```\n(buffer-minor-maps \" *minibuf-f-tgfe72q*\")\n; => (\"editing-state-map\" \"editing-caret-map\" \"cua-mode-map\")\n```\n\nLocals persist with the desktop, so anything stamped there is durable state. `dismiss-sync-visible!` is safe only by accident (it walks `window-list`).\n\n**3. `change` handlers are not wrapped.** Select, confirm and cancel go through `with-invoking-buffer` (`editor.scm:2873-2881`); `change` does not. 12 sites (`ibuffer.scm:965`, `jj.scm:415`, `project.scm:536`, `editor.scm:1812, 2744, 2799, 2811, 2845, 5955, 12257`), and only isearch (`editor.scm:5131`) guards itself with `with-window-buffer`. Those 3 isearch calls are the only uses of that escape hatch in the whole tree.\n\n**4. Mode and keymap installers that take the implicit buffer.** 41 `define-mode` bodies open with `(current-buffer)`. `collect-mode` (`editor.scm:2155-2161`) is reached *from* a live prompt (C-c C-o continues the prompt as a buffer) and ends in `(buffer-set-read-only! buf #t)`; `define-list-mode!` setup does the same at `editor.scm:8507`, plus `local-remap*!` of n/p. `local-set-key` and `local-remap!` write to current-buffer; the `*!` variants take a buffer.\n\n**5. Async continuations.** A lane, shell, LSP or fetch callback that lands while a prompt is open inherits the minibuf. `with-current-buffer` does override the redirect (`session.ex:2324`, `Frame.with_buffer`), so `restore-buffer-runtime!` is safe, but nothing forces callbacks to use it.\n\n**6. Write path.** `buffer-save!` with no argument and `write-file!` act on current-buffer. During a prompt that is the minibuffer, which pairs badly with the known save-clobber footgun.\n\n**7. Presentation keys off the flag alone.** `buffer-dismissible?` (`dismiss.scm:33`) needs only `buffer-read-only?`, so any buffer that ever gets flagged inherits `q` and the Reading bar. The guard belongs at the flag, not the bar.\n\nAlready safe, so no need to chase: plain `minibuffer-read` / `completing-read` confirm and cancel handlers run after `Editor.minibuffer_close()` (`session.ex:2634`), with the prompt gone.\n\nSmallest fix set: an unwind guard in `with-invoking-buffer`, wrap `change` the same way, and a `minibuffer-buffer?` refusal inside `buffer-set-read-only!` and `set-mode!`. Want me to make those three?"]],"role":"assistant"}]
